  "idioms": [
    {
      "id": "ṣyd.idiom.1",
      "raw": "ṣoyәd/zobәṭ qadr: to show respect/honor, hospitalit; Mṭalle lu ḥəmmam, masḥalle, malwaššalle ǧule naḏ̣ife, madmaxxe bayn aǧ ǧule w ṣəddalle qadr haqqa ‘They brought him to the bath, washed him, they clothed him in clean clothes, made him a (real) bed and they showed him great honor. And then in the morning the sultan of the city assigned him to a shop’.NE_Dilo_and_Falako",
      "headword": "ṣoyәd/zobәṭ qadr"
    }
  ],
